@CC1
Syntax: CC1 [<opts>] <file> [<file> ...] [<opts>]
Usage : Compile C source to an OS-9 module (two pass front end)
Files : <name>.c  C source        <name>.a  assembler source
        <name>.r  relocatable object (linked only)
Opts  :
  -d<name>   define preprocessor symbol <name>
  -c         keep preprocessor line-number directives
  -o         do not run the optimizer (c.opt)
  -p         generate profiling information
  -s         strip symbol information from the output
  -r         stop after the relocatable object (.r), do not link
  -a         stop after the assembler source (.a), do not assemble
  -f=<file>  name the final linked module <file>
  -n=<name>  set the output module name
  -e=<num>   set the module edition number
  -m=<size>  add <size> bytes of data memory
  -l=<path>  link with library <path> (up to 4)
  -x         build the command file but do not run it
Note  : option letters are not case sensitive.  CC1 drives the passes
        c.prep, c.pass1, c.pass2, c.opt, c.asm and c.link in turn.
